{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784147389,"nonce":"oaLX2hKZkET4I4LhmNQtThp+L+k=","title":"Give a Pipeline a typed **launch-parameter** declaration and bind supplied values end-to-end, proven through the existing inline `POST /v1/runs` path (World-B dispatch is a later slice). This is the foundation slice for ADR-0043: it makes `interface.inputs` a real *launch* contract, typed, validated, and interpolatable.","message":"Scope, end-to-end:\n- **Typed `interface.inputs`** — grow it from a list of names to a list of parameter specs: `{ name, type, required, default?, options?, validate?, description? }`. `type ∈ { string, boolean, number, choice }` (a closed vocabulary; `choice` carries `options`). Expand-only, version-stamped IR change (ADR-0022). Authors keep string-authored `with:` unchanged.\n- **Compile-time validation** — `required: true` ⇒ no `default`; `required: false` ⇒ `default` mandatory; `choice` ⇒ non-empty `options` and any `default` ∈ `options`; unique names; name safety. A bad declaration is a submit-time compile error (ADR-0009).\n- **One shared `coerce(raw: serde_json::Value, ty: ParamType) -\u003e Result\u003cTypedValue\u003e`** in the pure `scarab-pipeline` crate: `\"3\"`+number→`3`, already-typed passthrough, `\"yes\"`/`true`+boolean→`true`, value ∉ options + choice → error; then run the optional `validate:` CEL predicate (pure/total, fail-closed).\n- **Binding** — the resolved `name → typed value` map is frozen on the Run at creation (a `params` JSON blob on the run record, immutable). `inputs` joins the **existing** ADR-0041 CEL context, in scope **run-wide from creation** (so `${{ inputs.x }}` resolves in `image`/`command`/`env`/`when:` and in run-level `concurrency.group`). Unreferenced params still inject as `SCARAB_PARAM_\u003cNAME\u003e` env (the same convention `with:` uses). No new interpolation mechanism.\n- **Supply path (thin, temporary)** — extend inline `POST /v1/runs` to accept a `params` map; the server runs `coerce`+`validate` fail-closed before creating the run. This is only to make the slice demoable via API; the product dispatch path is slice 2.\n- **Restart determinism** — because params are frozen once, a restart (new Attempt) re-reads the identical map → byte-identical interpolation. Guard with one crash/resume test (protects the durability wedge).\n\n\n- [ ] `interface.inputs` accepts typed param specs; round-trips through IR (de)serialization; `ir_version` bumped, old IRs still load (ADR-0022).\n- [ ] Compile rejects: required-with-default, optional-without-default, empty/absent `choice` options, default ∉ options, duplicate/invalid names — each with a clear diagnostic.\n- [ ] `coerce` unit-tested across all four types for JSON-typed and string inputs, including failure cases; `validate:` CEL enforced fail-closed.\n- [ ] `POST /v1/runs` with a `params` map: required missing → rejected pre-run; supplied values coerced/validated; a resolved-once `params` blob persisted on the Run.\n- [ ] `${{ inputs.\u003cname\u003e }}` interpolates in step `image`/`command`/`env`/`when:` and in `concurrency.group`; typed guard (`inputs.n \u003e 80`) is numeric, not lexicographic.\n- [ ] `SCARAB_PARAM_\u003cNAME\u003e` injected for every declared param (referenced or not).\n- [ ] Crash/resume test: a run interpolating a param re-derives identical bytes after control-plane restart.\n- [ ] `dict` and `list` are not accepted as types (closed vocabulary).\n\n\nNone - can start immediately.","files":null}]}